## Question Number: 15

**The Question:** Consider two programs. Program A starts i at 1 and repeats until i > 10, displaying i then incrementing. Program B starts i at 0 and repeats until i ≥ 10, incrementing i then displaying. Which of the following best compares the values displayed by programs A and B?

**My Answer:** D - Program B displays one more value than program A.

**Correct Answer:** A - Program A and program B display identical values in the same order.

**My Reflection:** I didn't trace through both programs carefully. Program A: i starts at 1, displays i (1), then increments - so it displays 1, 2, 3, ..., 10. Program B: i starts at 0, increments first (i becomes 1), then displays - so it also displays 1, 2, 3, ..., 10. Both programs print exactly ten values (1 through 10) in the same order. The different starting values and loop conditions compensate for the different order of operations inside the loop. I need to fully trace loops instead of making assumptions about their output.

