## Question Number: 50

**The Question:** Consider three algorithms operating on a list of n elements: I accesses each element twice, II accesses each element n times, III accesses only the first 10 elements. Which run in reasonable time?

**My Answer:** B - III only

**Correct Answer:** D - I, II, and III

**My Reflection:** I had too narrow a definition of "reasonable time." In AP CSP, an algorithm runs in reasonable time if it runs in polynomial time (or better). Algorithm I runs in O(2n) = O(n) time - linear and reasonable. Algorithm II runs in O(n²) time - polynomial and still reasonable. Algorithm III runs in O(10) = O(1) time - constant and reasonable. All three are polynomial, so all run in reasonable time. Only exponential or worse algorithms (like O(2ⁿ)) are considered unreasonable. I need to remember that polynomial includes linear, quadratic, cubic, etc.

