## Question Number: 63

**The Question:** A bookstore database has columns: Author, Title, Selling Price, Genre, and Quantity Available. An employee wants to calculate total revenue from selling all available science fiction books. Which two columns can be ignored and still allow this calculation? (Select two.)

**My Answer:** I selected B (Title) but missed the second correct answer.

**Correct Answer:** A (Author) and B (Title)

**My Reflection:** I correctly identified that Title is not needed for the calculation, but I failed to also select Author. To calculate total revenue for science fiction books, the employee needs Genre (to filter for science fiction), Selling Price (to know the price per book), and Quantity Available (to know how many to sell). That means both Author and Title are irrelevant to the calculation and can be ignored. I need to think through which columns are actually required for the computation and then select all remaining columns as ignorable.

